        "timestamp": 1774422684,
        "contenuto_esteso": "Democrats projected to win back Florida district home to Trump's Mar-a-Lago Americas The US Democratic Party appears to have won back a Florida state legislative from the Republicans – and one that's home to US President Donald Trump's lavish Mar-a-Lago estate. Issued on: 25/03/2026 - 08:11 Modified: 25/03/2026 - 08:11 1 min Reading time US Democrats were projected Tuesday to have flipped a Florida legislative seat in a district that included US President Donald Trump 's Mar-a-Lago estate as part of a special election carrying symbolic weight. Emily Gregory, a first-time candidate, was on course to beat a Trump-backed Republican rival to win the Florida District 87 state-level House seat that includes Trump's opulent Florida home, CNN and the New York Times projected . \"Congratulations to Emily Gregory on her election to represent House District 87!\" the Florida Democratic Party \"Democrats just flipped Trump's home seat and Mar-a-lago!\" To display this content from X (Twitter), you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. The Republicans continue to hold a supermajority in the Florida state legislature. Gregory's projected win follows a trend of Democratic wins over Republicans across the United States in recent months. In what analysts have pointed to as evidence of voters' growing disenchantment with the Republican Party, a Democratic candidate won a state Senate seat in a traditionally Republican stronghold in Texas in January. That followed a series of Democratic Party wins last fall with New Jersey and Virginia electing Democratic governors and left-wing Zohran Mamdani sweeping to power in New York City's mayoral election. The upcoming US midterm elections set for November are shaping up to pose a challenge to the Republican majority in Congress amid economic pressures and the risks of a prolonged conflict in Iran . (FRANCE 24 with AFP)"
